    {
      "id": "happy",
      "tab": "Happy path",
      "short": "Publish, reserve, ack, run",
      "q": "With the defaults, a worker reserves several messages and acks each one just before it runs",
      "frames": [
        {
          "clock": "0:00",
          "badge": "3 messages on the queue",
          "term": ">>> send_email.delay(user_id)   # × 3\n# each call becomes a message; nothing has run yet",
          "queue": [
            {
              "id": "T1",
              "st": "new",
              "meta": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "T2",
              "st": "new",
              "meta": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "T3",
              "st": "new",
              "meta": ""
            }
          ],
          "unacked": [],
          "workers": [
            {
              "n": "worker A",
              "conc": 2,
              "limit": 8,
              "slots": [null, null],
              "buf": [],
              "note": "concurrency 2 · may reserve up to 2 × 4 = 8",
              "st": ""
            }
          ],
          "done": [],
          "on": ["broker"],
          "h": "Publish",
          "b": "Each <code>.delay()</code> call is serialized into a message and put on the queue. The app moves on; nothing has run."
        },
        {
          "clock": "0:00",
          "badge": "reserved: in A's buffer, unacked in the broker",
          "queue": [],
          "unacked": [
            {
              "id": "T1",
              "st": "new",
              "meta": "delivered to A"
            },
            {
              "id": "T2",
              "st": "new",
              "meta": "delivered to A"
            },
            {
              "id": "T3",
              "st": "new",
              "meta": "delivered to A"
            }
          ],
          "workers": [
            {
              "n": "worker A",
              "conc": 2,
              "limit": 8,
              "slots": [null, null],
              "buf": [
                {
                  "id": "T1",
                  "st": "new",
                  "meta": ""
                },
                {
                  "id": "T2",
                  "st": "new",
                  "meta": ""
                },
                {
                  "id": "T3",
                  "st": "new",
                  "meta": ""
                }
              ],
              "note": "reserved 3 of its 8 slots",
              "st": ""
            }
          ],
          "done": [],
          "on": ["worker A", "broker"],
          "h": "Reserve",
          "b": "The worker asks for messages and receives all three, since it may hold up to 8. They leave the queue and sit in its prefetch buffer. In the broker they are delivered but not yet acknowledged."
        },
        {
          "clock": "0:00",
          "badge": "ack, then run",
          "queue": [],
          "unacked": [
            {
              "id": "T3",
              "st": "",
              "meta": "delivered to A"
            }
          ],
          "workers": [
            {
              "n": "worker A",
              "conc": 2,
              "limit": 8,
              "slots": [
                {
                  "id": "T1",
                  "st": "new",
                  "meta": ""
                },
                {
                  "id": "T2",
                  "st": "new",
                  "meta": ""
                }
              ],
              "buf": [
                {
                  "id": "T3",
                  "st": "",
                  "meta": ""
                }
              ],
              "note": "acked T1 and T2 just before running them",
              "st": ""
            }
          ],
          "done": [],
          "on": ["worker A"],
          "h": "Ack, then run",
          "b": "For T1 and T2, the worker acknowledges each message just before handing it to a free process, and the broker forgets them. T3 waits in the buffer for a free process."
        },
        {
          "clock": "0:02",
          "badge": "\"acknowledged\" means \"started\", not \"finished\"",
          "queue": [],
          "unacked": [],
          "workers": [
            {
              "n": "worker A",
              "conc": 2,
              "limit": 8,
              "slots": [
                {
                  "id": "T3",
                  "st": "new",
                  "meta": ""
                },
                null
              ],
              "buf": [],
              "note": "acked T3 and started it",
              "st": ""
            }
          ],
          "done": [
            {
              "id": "T1",
              "st": "new",
              "meta": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "T2",
              "st": "new",
              "meta": ""
            }
          ],
          "on": ["worker A"],
          "h": "Done",
          "b": "T1 and T2 finish; T3 is acknowledged and starts. Nothing is left in the broker. By default, the broker forgot each task when it started, not when it finished."
        }
      ],
      "take": "By default, \"acknowledged\" means \"started\", not \"finished\". Prefetching trades fairness between workers for fewer broker round trips.",
      "gen": "Consumer prefetch (QoS) in AMQP, SQS receive-then-delete, and Kafka consumer batching: the client holds work before doing it, and the ack decides what survives a crash."
    },
