          "h": "Only the child process dies",
          "b": "If the task's process is killed but the worker survives, the worker acknowledges the message even with late acks, so it isn't retried. <code>task_reject_on_worker_lost = True</code> re-queues it instead."
        }
      ],
      "take": "Choose between at most once (early ack, can lose tasks) and at least once (late ack, can repeat tasks). With late acks, make tasks idempotent: an idempotency key with the payment provider, or a state check before charging.",
      "gen": "Delivery guarantees in every queue: auto versus manual ack in RabbitMQ, deleting an SQS message before or after processing, committing Kafka offsets before or after processing."
    },
